Had a quite good game started yesterday; lost it due to putting down an
elven mithril coat for price ID in a shop (and selling my bronze plate
mail), then going out, taking off the cloak, wanting to put the mithril
on, remembering, entering the shop – well, trying to enter.  Both suits
of armor gone.  Such errors do make the convict hard.

The food restriction at the beginning might be a motive not to include
it in Nethack 4.0 – devnull-like callenges "with bells on" [1] will
become much more random if it isn't granted that your character won't
starve at the first few moves.  I had a game where I killed 4-5 eligible
monsters, none of which left a corpse…  Luck and prayer also don't help
here, of course.  Of course, you could always _start_ with the convict.

One thing appears a bit strange to me:  Kobolds cannot be eaten safely
(they are poisonous), but kobold zombies are OK (they only get you ill,
which doesn't affect the convict).  Is this intended, i.e. is rising as
a zombie supposed to alter the body's cellular substance?

Again in 0.5, I saw a miner at the level with the mines stairs.  Wasn't
this taken out?  Maybe forgot a fallthrough somewhere…?  Actually, I
find them fitting in the mines, so I'd leave them there.

Entering the first level of the mines for a short time proved very
beneficial – solved the food problem, got me very good armor and a few
XP levels.  The iron ball kills the gnomes and dwarfs quickly enough,
when it doesn't miss.  So I didn't yet (mines level 1) find the mines
considerably harder than with other roles.  On the opposite, the game
got quite a bit easier for me at that point.

